// Practice quiz: Reading: how auto-configuration works
// Minimum release, November 2026: author-checked, no independent review. Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: spring-boot/spring-boot-basics/how-auto-configuration-works

::o1 annotation parts::Which annotation does @SpringBootApplication include to turn on scanning? {
=@ComponentScan#Correct. It scans from the package of the annotated class.
~@EnableScheduling#Not quite. That is a separate feature.
~@RestController#Not quite. That is a stereotype for web handlers.
~@Transactional#Not quite. That concerns transactions.
}

::o2 missing bean condition::What does a missing-bean condition do when you have defined your own bean of that type? {
=It stops the auto-configured bean being created#Correct. It backs off in favor of yours.
~It replaces your bean#Not quite. Your bean is kept.
~It fails startup#Not quite. Backing off is the normal outcome.
~It creates a second bean anyway#Not quite. That would defeat the condition.
}

::o2 classpath condition::A class-based condition checks for a class that is not on the classpath. What happens? {
=That auto-configuration does not apply#Correct. No class, no feature; it is reported as a negative match.
~Boot downloads the class#Not quite. Nothing is downloaded at startup.
~Startup always fails#Not quite. Skipping is the normal result.
~The bean is created with null fields#Not quite. The bean is not created at all.
}

::o3 debug report::Which option prints the conditions evaluation report at startup? {
=Starting with the --debug argument#Correct. Setting debug\=true also works.
~Setting server.port#Not quite. That changes the port.
~The Maven test goal#Not quite. Tests do not print this report by default.
~Adding @Bean to main#Not quite. That is unrelated.
}

::o3 reading the report::In the report, where do you look to find why a feature was skipped? {
=Negative matches#Correct. That section lists each condition that failed.
~Positive matches#Not quite. Those applied.
~The startup banner#Not quite. It has no condition detail.
~The port line#Not quite. It only reports the server port.
}

